  "name": "magma-trail",
  "vibe": "Basalt #1f1a18 and bone under a lava #f43f1e that only owns a whole frame on the Statement beat; ember #ffa03c and an ash grey do the rest. Bevan's heavy slab caps slam in at 2.2x scale with a four-degree kick. The backdrop is a working volcano and it is deliberately slow: an ash-grey crater silhouette fills the lower frame, a lava tongue at the lip pulses on a sine, four bombs arc out of the vent and fall on a ballistic curve, three ash plumes rise and thin over five seconds, ember heat-shimmer squiggles drift upward, and a lava-dashed ridgeline crawls along the bottom like a waymarked route. Its beats are field kit — a needle gauge for crater temp, dotted-leader ledger boards, alerts that drop in from above, and an odometer word roll.",
